+## Saved knowledge
+
+Outside topology and hold modes, only the EA receives `memory_search(query?)`, `memory_get(id)`, and `memory_propose(scope, key, kind, text, source, expires_at_ms?)`. Workers cannot call them. Scope identities come from runtime context; project scope requires an operator link.
+
+Search returns bounded recall; an empty query selects preferences and decisions. Get returns the current revision and provenance, including the EA's own candidate. Propose returns the saved status: `confirmed` by default or `candidate` when review is enabled. Identical retries with a stable key are safe; corrections require operator revision checks. Memory arguments and errors are redacted in MCP debug logs. See [state and recovery](state-and-recovery.md) for storage and visibility rules.
+
